{"parentUuid":"d482e560-716e-426c-8fa8-7aec3c0d0547","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Plain"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2a744846-5ee7-47fd-9bef-2299c81c1f91","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:35:52.743Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","hash":"a9edd97b576cacfcdf2b14892c1f4639fc285e1ec8086a5ed2840320307fd479","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NrriNWrnLkQ8kVfBDhHYVz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFirst launch: ask which printer on a screen of its own, bring OrcaSlicer's ticked printers, and show a skipped printer as \"No printer yet\"\n\nThe Printers step showed the add-printer dialog standing alone, with its own\nstep counter and four ways out. It is now a screen: \"Which printer do you\nhave?\", the dialog's Brand, Model and Nozzle fields (moved into a shared\nPrinterPicker that the dialog also uses), Continue, Skip for now, the\nOrcaSlicer folder link and Back. Continue adds the printer with its\nprofile's default plate and filament. \"Can't find your printer? Ask the\nagent\" finishes onboarding and opens the printer chat when the agent can\nanswer (an account with credits, or a saved key). Back after the OrcaSlicer\nscreen's Start fresh returns to that screen.\n\nThe OrcaSlicer screen and the printer screen open with what the welcome\nfinished: \"Signed in as ... · N credits\", or \"The agent uses your <provider>\nkey\".\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import also reads the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer\nlist and the one it has selected (OrcaSlicer.conf \"models\" and \"presets\"),\nmapped to JusPrin's own profiles, skipping any a saved preset is based on.\nEach is installed and saved as a printer of its own; OrcaSlicer's selected\nprinter ends up selected. A failed one shows as not imported and Retry\ninstalls it again.\n\nSkipping now saves the default as \"Generic printer\", which the printer chip\nnames \"Generic printer · 0.4\". Home shows it as a \"No printer yet\" card with\n\"Add your printer\" instead of a printer card marked \"assumed\", hides the\n\"+ Add printer\" row while it shows, and stops listing it once the person\nadds a printer of their own.\nEOF\ngit log -1 --format='%h %s'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
